Fixed. The bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check compared URLs with `===`, which is case-sensitive for the hostname, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` never matched.

**Change:** match on `normalizeUrl(b.url) === normalizeUrl(inc.url)` instead of raw `b.url === inc.url`, reusing the repo's existing `normalizeUrl` (which lowercases the hostname and strips tracking params).

**Verified** (Deno, run in the disposable run root):
- hostname case-diff → single entry, tags unioned: `["example.com/a", ["existing","imported"]]` ✓
- identical URL → tags unioned ✓
- different URL → appended unchanged ✓

Type-checks clean under `deno.json` (the `.ts` import extension is intentional to the project). No existing test suite covers `mergeImports`, so I added an inline check rather than committing a test to the fixture.


